/**
  @page guides-meshes-queries Geometric queries
  @brief Interpret dimensions, entity counts, measures and attributes.

  @tableofcontents
  @m_footernavigation

  @section guides-meshes-queries-intro Query the stored mesh

  A query acts on the mesh's current entities and geometry. Compute the
  required incidence relations before querying facets or boundaries. The
  `MeshBasics` example uses a rectangle of width two and height one, split
  into two triangles and one quadrilateral.

  @section guides-meshes-queries-basic Dimensions and counts

  @subsection guides-meshes-queries-basic-dim Dimensions

  `getDimension()` is the topological cell dimension; `getSpaceDimension()`
  is the embedding dimension. A surface mesh in three-dimensional space has
  dimensions two and three respectively.

  @subsection guides-meshes-queries-basic-counts Counts

  `getVertexCount()`, `getFaceCount()` and `getCellCount()` count vertices,
  codimension-one facets and cells. `getPolytopeCount(d)` selects a dimension;
  its geometry-type overload selects a reference shape. Counts of discovered
  edges and faces depend on which incidence relations have been computed.

  @subsection guides-meshes-queries-basic-empty Empty meshes

  `isEmpty()` tests whether a mesh contains cells. Check it before computing
  an average or evaluating a quantity that requires a cell.

  @section guides-meshes-queries-geometric Select the measure dimension

  | Query | Entities included |
  | :--- | :--- |
  | `getMeasure(d)` | All stored entities of dimension `d` |
  | `getArea()` | All two-dimensional entities |
  | `getVolume()` | All three-dimensional entities |
  | `getPerimeter()` | Boundary facets of the mesh |

  @subsection guides-meshes-queries-geometric-volume Volume

  A volume mesh has three-dimensional cells. `getVolume()` sums their
  geometric measures. Its attribute overloads restrict that sum to selected
  three-dimensional entities.

  @subsection guides-meshes-queries-geometric-area Area

  On a planar or surface mesh, `getArea()` sums cell areas. In a volume mesh,
  it sums all stored faces, including interior faces. Boundary surface area
  is obtained from `getPerimeter()` after computing facet-to-cell incidence.

  @subsection guides-meshes-queries-geometric-perimeter Boundary measure

  `getPerimeter()` measures the lengths of boundary facets in a two-dimensional
  mesh and their areas in a three-dimensional mesh. Attribute overloads select
  boundary-facet labels.

  @subsection guides-meshes-queries-geometric-measure Generic measure

  `mesh.getMeasure(mesh.getDimension())` sums the cell measures in the mesh's
  own dimension. Summing dimension-one entities of a triangular mesh includes
  its interior edges as well as its boundary edges.

  @snippet Geometry/MeshBasics.cpp mesh-basics-queries

  Expected values are six vertices, eight edges, three cells, area two,
  perimeter six and area one in each region.

  @section guides-meshes-queries-attributes Optional attributes

  @subsection guides-meshes-queries-attributes-get Read a label

  An entity may have no attribute. `getAttribute()`, `getCellAttribute(i)` and
  `getFaceAttribute(i)` therefore return an optional value. Test presence
  before dereferencing it.

  @snippet Geometry/MeshBasics.cpp mesh-basics-iterate

  @subsection guides-meshes-queries-attributes-set Set a label

  `mesh.setAttribute({dimension, index}, value)` labels one entity. Region
  labels belong to cells; boundary-condition labels belong to facets. A cell
  label does not automatically label its boundary facets.

  @section guides-meshes-queries-spatial Coordinates and boundaries

  @subsection guides-meshes-queries-spatial-coords Vertex coordinates

  `mesh.getVertexCoordinates(i)` returns the coordinates of vertex `i`.
  The coordinate vector has `getSpaceDimension()` entries. For points inside
  a cell, construct a `Geometry::Point` from a cell and reference coordinates.

  @subsection guides-meshes-queries-spatial-surface Surface meshes

  `isSurface()` tests the mesh's surface classification. Compare the two
  dimensions when the embedding codimension itself is needed.

  @subsection guides-meshes-queries-spatial-boundary Boundary facets

  After computing facet-to-cell connectivity, `isBoundary(faceIndex)` selects
  facets with one incident cell. `isInterface(faceIndex)` selects interior
  facets; attribute jumps can be selected separately through region labels.

  @section guides-meshes-queries-example Checked program

  Build and run `MeshBasics` from a scratch directory. It compares the reported
  measures with analytic rectangle and cube-surface values and returns
  `EXIT_FAILURE` if the checks fail.

  @section guides-meshes-queries-see-also Continue

  - @ref guides-meshes-iteration "Iteration and optional attributes"
  - @ref guides-meshes-connectivity "Incidence prerequisites"
  - @ref Geometry/MeshBasics.cpp "Complete checked source"

  @example Geometry/MeshBasics.cpp
*/
